  "question": {
    "text": "In an aqueous solution, the ionization constants for carbonic acid are<br />\r<br />\r<math><mrow><msub><mtext>K</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>4.2</mtext> <mo>×</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>&nbsp;K</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>4.8</mtext> <mo>×</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>11</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br />\r<br />\rSelect the correct statement for a saturated <math> <mrow> <mtext>0.034 M</mtext> </mrow> </math> solution of the carbonic acid:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
